# Shell scripts must always have LF line endings — a shebang script with
# CRLF fails at runtime inside Linux containers ("illegal option -",
# "invalid option") since the shell parses the trailing \r as part of the
# preceding token. This bit both docker/db-backup/backup.sh and
# docker/db-init/10-restore-if-exists.sh on first production deploy
# (2026-09-17): `git archive` on a Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true
# converts LF -> CRLF in its output even though the stored git blob itself
# was LF, so this must be enforced here rather than assumed from what the
# local working tree or `git show` looks like.
*.sh text eol=lf
